34:- one primary skill = task-shaped execution pack
38:`AGENTS.md -> one base prompt -> needed overlays -> one primary skill -> optional example packet`
52:   - orchestration / lifecycle / delegation
53:2. select one primary skill based on that dominant control problem, not on the richest available surface
60:- do not stack multiple primary skills at once
61:- if the dominant control problem changes, reroute instead of accreting more structure
62:- if the same low-gain loop repeats, checkpoint, reroute, or stop rather than narrating the whole loop
69:Choose one primary skill first.
111:- `PROMPT_multi_agent_overlay` when decomposition or A2A is itself part of the recommendation
162:### 2.5 `orchestration-control`
165:- multi-agent or A2A coordination is the main execution problem
175:- `orchestration-control`
180:- `PROMPT_retrieval_grounding_overlay` when capability discovery or orchestration decisions depend on grounded external evidence
191:### 2.7 Primary-skill reroute cue
193:Reroute the primary skill when the problem shape changes:
194:- from `coding-core` to `orchestration-control` when coordination, async lifecycle, or delegated integration becomes the main problem rather than incidental implementation
196:- from any primary skill to `eval-ops` when the real question becomes release gating, regression judgment, or monitored continuation
200:- one primary skill at a time
201:- reroute when the center of gravity changes
204:### 2.8 Prompt-stack guide reflection / benchmark maintenance
226:- `Guide reflection benchmark memo` for question -> answer -> verification -> patch-target loops
240:- final ownership reroutes to `eval-ops` once the decision depends on replay execution state, benchmark gating, or release-sensitive continuation rather than route comparison alone
284:- A2A lifecycle-aware collaboration -> `A2A task-handoff memo`
289:- guide-chapter reflection or doc-to-runtime parity benchmark -> `Guide reflection benchmark memo`
324:When Codex is maintaining reflection against a governing guide, use these anchor routes:
328:- Parallelization / Multi-Agent / A2A -> `PROMPT_multi_agent_overlay` + `orchestration-control`; prefer `Delegation admission memo`, `A2A task-handoff memo`, and `Join-quality review memo`
335:- Appendix A / advanced prompting execution families -> `PROMPT_search_reasoning_overlay` for decomposition, step-back, self-consistency, ReAct-like loops, tree-style search, and bounded reflection; keep prompt chaining in base prompts and treat example-catalog references as structure-only
337:- Evaluation / Monitoring -> `PROMPT_evaluation_monitoring_overlay` + `eval-ops`; prefer `Benchmark registry memo`, `Guide reflection benchmark memo`, or `Prompt-stack release review`
340:- if a chapter family can only be answered by operator-facing prose and not by the active runtime / skill surface, treat that as a reflection gap and patch the actual prompt docs before claiming parity
351:- keep guide / runtime / skill lookup parity visible for goal, recovery, approval, budget, prioritization, readiness, and lifecycle-audit packets; do not let one layer silently know a family the others no longer expose
422:Use one primary skill.
